-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, s 262(g) to (l) -- THE APPRAISAL PROCEEDING IN THE COURT OF CHANCERY.
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N.
--
-- Subsection (g) is the hearing on who is entitled (and the Court's power to dismiss, including the de minimis dismissal of a
-- listed class); (h) the valuation and interest; (i) the direction to pay; (j) costs and expenses; (k) the position of the person
-- who has demanded appraisal (no vote, no dividends, withdrawal, lapse); (l) the status of the shares that would have been issued.
--
-- The Court of Chancery has no seat. Everything it decides ("the Court shall determine", "the Court may", "in its discretion")
-- is a judgment handed to someone else, so each rule takes the Court's finding or order as a plain input and says what follows
-- for the person (what may be done to them, what they must be paid, what they may require). Money is in dollars; shares and
-- holders are counted as NUMBERs; a rate is a fraction of 1.

§ `s 262(g) The hearing on who is entitled, and dismissal`

-- "At the hearing on such petition, the Court shall determine the persons who have complied with this section and who have become
-- entitled to appraisal rights." The determination is the Court's: it is the input; the rules of subsections (a) to (f) say what it
-- ought to be.
-- src:1269 | At the hearing on such petition, the Court shall determine the persons who have complied with this section and who have become entitled to appraisal rights …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(g) (src:1269)
GIVEN `the Court has determined that the person has complied with this section and has become entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(g) the person is one of the persons the Court has determined to be entitled to appraisal rights` `the Court has determined that the person has complied with this section and has become entitled to appraisal rights` MEANS
    `the Court has determined that the person has complied with this section and has become entitled to appraisal rights`

-- "The Court may require the persons who have demanded an appraisal for their shares and who hold stock represented by
-- certificates to submit their certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery for notation thereon of the pendency of the
-- appraisal proceedings; and if any person fails to comply with such direction, the Court may dismiss the proceedings as to such person."
-- src:1269 | The Court may require the persons who have demanded an appraisal for their shares and who hold stock represented by certificates to submit their certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery for notation thereon of the pendency of the appraisal proceedings; and if any person fails to comply with such direction, the Court may dismiss the proceedings as to such person …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(g) (src:1269)
GIVEN `the person has demanded an appraisal for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds stock represented by certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed the person to submit the certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(g) the Court may dismiss the proceedings as to the person for not submitting certificates` `the person has demanded an appraisal for the shares` `the person holds stock represented by certificates` `the Court has directed the person to submit the certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery` `the person has failed to comply with the direction` MEANS
        `the person has demanded an appraisal for the shares`
    AND `the person holds stock represented by certificates`
    AND `the Court has directed the person to submit the certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery`
    AND `the person has failed to comply with the direction`

-- The de minimis dismissal. "If immediately before the merger ... the shares of the class or series ... as to which appraisal rights are
-- available were listed on a national securities exchange, the Court shall dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of such shares
-- who are otherwise entitled to appraisal rights unless (1) the total number of shares entitled to appraisal exceeds 1% of the
-- outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal, (2) the value of the consideration provided in the merger ... for
-- such total number of shares exceeds $1 million, or (3) the merger was approved pursuant to s 253 or s 267."
-- If the shares were not listed immediately before the transaction, this sentence does not apply and answers FALSE (no mandatory
-- dismissal). NOTHING (not covered) for counts that cannot be: no outstanding shares eligible, or more shares entitled than
-- are outstanding.
-- src:1269 | If immediately before the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance the shares of the class or series of stock of the constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation as to which appraisal rights are available were listed on a national securities exchange, the Court shall dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of such shares who are otherwise entitled to appraisal rights unless (1) the total number of shares entitled to appraisal exceeds 1% of the outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal, (2) the value of the consideration provided in the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance for such total number of shares exceeds $1 million, or (3) the merger was approved pursuant to § 253 or § 267 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(g) (src:1269)
DECLARE `s 262(g) Shares seeking appraisal` HAS
    `the shares were listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the transaction`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the value of the consideration provided in the transaction for such total number of shares`            IS A NUMBER   -- dollars
    `the merger was approved pursuant to s 253 or s 267`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1269 | If immediately before the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance the shares of the class or series of stock of the constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation as to which appraisal rights are available were listed on a national securities exchange, the Court shall dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of such shares who are otherwise entitled to appraisal rights unless (1) the total number of shares entitled to appraisal exceeds 1% of the outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal, (2) the value of the consideration provided in the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance for such total number of shares exceeds $1 million, or (3) the merger was approved pursuant to § 253 or § 267 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(g) (src:1269)
GIVEN s IS A `s 262(g) Shares seeking appraisal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(g) the Court must dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of the shares` s MEANS
    IF NOT s's `the shares were listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the transaction`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF       s's `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal` AT MOST 0
               OR s's `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal` LESS THAN 0
               OR s's `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal` GREATER THAN s's `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (NOT (       s's `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal` GREATER THAN (s's `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal` TIMES 1%)
                          OR s's `the value of the consideration provided in the transaction for such total number of shares` GREATER THAN 1_000_000
                          OR s's `the merger was approved pursuant to s 253 or s 267`))

§ `s 262(h) Valuation, interest and participation`

-- "Through such proceeding the Court shall determine the fair value of the shares exclusive of any element of value arising from
-- the accomplishment or expectation of the merger ..., together with interest, if any, to be paid upon the amount determined to be the
-- fair value. In determining such fair value, the Court shall take into account all relevant factors." The Court's findings are
-- the inputs: the value of the shares and the element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction.
-- src:1270 | Through such proceeding the Court shall determine the fair value of the shares exclusive of any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, together with interest, if any, to be paid upon the amount determined to be the fair value. In determining such fair value, the Court shall take into account all relevant factors …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(h) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the value of the shares including any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction` IS A NUMBER
      `the element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 262(h) the fair value of the shares` `the value of the shares including any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction` `the element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction` MEANS
    `the value of the shares including any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction` MINUS `the element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction`

-- The interest. "Unless the Court in its discretion determines otherwise for good cause shown, and except as provided in this
-- subsection, interest from the effective date ... through the date of payment of the judgment shall be compounded quarterly and shall
-- accrue at 5% over the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge) as established from time to time during the period".
-- Reading F-h1: "5% over" is 5 percentage points over the discount rate; the rate is a rate per year, so each whole quarter accrues one
-- quarter of it, (rate + 5%) / 4, compounded quarter by quarter on the running total. The text says neither "per annum" nor how a part
-- of a quarter accrues, so the rule answers only for whole quarters: NOTHING (not covered) if any days of a part-quarter remain.
-- If the Court determines otherwise for good cause shown, the interest is whatever it determines: the input.
-- src:1270 | Unless the Court in its discretion determines otherwise for good cause shown, and except as provided in this subsection, interest from the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance through the date of payment of the judgment …
-- src:1270 | shall be compounded quarterly and shall accrue at 5% over the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge) as established from time to time during the period between the effective date of the merger, consolidation or conversion and the date of payment of the judgment …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(h) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the fair value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest the Court determined otherwise for good cause shown` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge) in force during each whole quarter` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the number of days of any part of a quarter after the last whole quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 262(h) the interest on the fair value` `the fair value of the shares` `the interest the Court determined otherwise for good cause shown` `the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge) in force during each whole quarter` `the number of days of any part of a quarter after the last whole quarter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the interest the Court determined otherwise for good cause shown`
    WHEN JUST courtsInterest THEN JUST courtsInterest
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the number of days of any part of a quarter after the last whole quarter` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the fair value of the shares` TIMES ((product (map (GIVEN rate YIELD 1 PLUS ((rate PLUS 5%) DIVIDED BY 4)) `the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge) in force during each whole quarter`)) MINUS 1))

-- "At any time before the entry of judgment in the proceedings, the surviving, resulting or converted entity may pay to each person
-- entitled to appraisal an amount in cash, in which case interest shall accrue thereafter as provided herein only upon the sum of (1)
-- the difference, if any, between the amount so paid and the fair value of the shares as determined by the Court, and (2) interest
-- theretofore accrued, unless paid at that time."
-- src:1270 | At any time before the entry of judgment in the proceedings, the surviving, resulting or converted entity may pay to each person entitled to appraisal an amount in cash, in which case interest shall accrue thereafter as provided herein only upon the sum of (1) the difference, if any, between the amount so paid and the fair value of the shares as determined by the Court, and (2) interest theretofore accrued, unless paid at that time …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(h) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the fair value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid in cash` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest accrued to the time of payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the accrued interest was paid at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 262(h) the sum on which interest accrues after a payment in cash` `the fair value of the shares` `the amount paid in cash` `the interest accrued to the time of payment` `the accrued interest was paid at that time` MEANS
    (max 0 (`the fair value of the shares` MINUS `the amount paid in cash`))
        PLUS (IF `the accrued interest was paid at that time` THEN 0 ELSE `the interest accrued to the time of payment`)

-- "Upon application by the surviving, resulting or converted entity or by any person entitled to participate in the appraisal
-- proceeding, the Court may, in its discretion, proceed to trial upon the appraisal prior to the final determination of the persons
-- entitled to an appraisal." Who may apply; the Court's discretion to grant is its own.
-- src:1270 | Upon application by the surviving, resulting or converted entity or by any person entitled to participate in the appraisal proceeding, the Court may, in its discretion, proceed to trial upon the appraisal prior to the final determination of the persons entitled to an appraisal …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(h) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the applicant is the surviving, resulting or converted entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person entitled to participate in the appraisal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(h) the applicant may apply for trial before the persons entitled are finally determined` `the applicant is the surviving, resulting or converted entity` `the applicant is a person entitled to participate in the appraisal proceeding` MEANS
        `the applicant is the surviving, resulting or converted entity`
    OR `the applicant is a person entitled to participate in the appraisal proceeding`

-- "Any person whose name appears on the list filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity pursuant to subsection (f) of
-- this section may participate fully in all proceedings until it is finally determined that such person is not entitled to appraisal
-- rights under this section."
-- src:1270 | Any person whose name appears on the list filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity pursuant to subsection (f) of this section may participate fully in all proceedings until it is finally determined that such person is not entitled to appraisal rights under this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(h) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has finally been determined that the person is not entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(h) the person may participate fully in all proceedings` `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` `it has finally been determined that the person is not entitled to appraisal rights` MEANS
        `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)`
    AND (NOT `it has finally been determined that the person is not entitled to appraisal rights`)

§ `s 262(i) The direction to pay`

-- "The Court shall direct the payment of the fair value of the shares, together with interest, if any, by the surviving, resulting or
-- converted entity to the persons entitled thereto." Not covered (NOTHING) where the interest is not covered.
-- src:1271 | The Court shall direct the payment of the fair value of the shares, together with interest, if any, by the surviving, resulting or converted entity to the persons entitled thereto …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(i) (src:1271)
GIVEN `the fair value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest on the fair value` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 262(i) the amount the Court directs the entity to pay the person` `the fair value of the shares` `the interest on the fair value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the interest on the fair value`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST interest THEN JUST (`the fair value of the shares` PLUS interest)

-- "The Court's decree may be enforced as other decrees in the Court of Chancery may be enforced, whether such surviving, resulting
-- or converted entity be an entity of this State or of any state." An entity of another jurisdiction of the United States is read
-- as an entity "of any state" (fork F-i1). An entity formed outside the United States is not within the words: NOTHING (not covered).
-- src:1271 | The Court’s decree may be enforced as other decrees in the Court of Chancery may be enforced, whether such surviving, resulting or converted entity be an entity of this State or of any state …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(i) (src:1271)
GIVEN w IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(i) the decree may be enforced as other decrees of the Court of Chancery are enforced` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `this State`                                  THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another jurisdiction of the United States`   THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` THEN NOTHING

§ `s 262(j) Costs and expenses`

-- "The costs of the proceeding may be determined by the Court and taxed upon the parties as the Court deems equitable in the
-- circumstances." Who can be taxed: a party. The Court's view of what is equitable is its own: the input.
-- src:1272 | The costs of the proceeding may be determined by the Court and taxed upon the parties as the Court deems equitable in the circumstances …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(j) (src:1272)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court deems it equitable in the circumstances to tax costs upon the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(j) the costs of the proceeding may be taxed upon the person` `the person is a party to the proceeding` `the Court deems it equitable in the circumstances to tax costs upon the person` MEANS
        `the person is a party to the proceeding`
    AND `the Court deems it equitable in the circumstances to tax costs upon the person`

-- "Upon application of a person whose name appears on the list filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity pursuant to
-- subsection (f) who participated in the proceeding and incurred expenses in connection therewith, the Court may order all or a
-- portion of such expenses, including, without limitation, reasonable attorney's fees and the fees and expenses of experts, to be
-- charged pro rata against the value of all the shares entitled to an appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject
-- to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction under subsection (k)."
-- src:1272 | Upon application of a person whose name appears on the list filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity pursuant to subsection (f) of this section who participated in the proceeding and incurred expenses in connection therewith …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(j) (src:1272)
GIVEN `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participated in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person incurred expenses in connection with the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(j) the person may apply for an order that expenses be charged against the shares` `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` `the person participated in the proceeding` `the person incurred expenses in connection with the proceeding` MEANS
        `the person's name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)`
    AND `the person participated in the proceeding`
    AND `the person incurred expenses in connection with the proceeding`

-- The pro rata charge. The Court orders "all or a portion" (the amount ordered is the Court's: the input); the charge is spread
-- over the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal that were not dismissed under (k) or that are subject to such an award
-- under a reservation of jurisdiction. A person's share of the charge is the amount ordered times the value of the person's
-- shares over that total. NOTHING (not covered) where the total is not positive or the person's shares are worth more than the total.
-- src:1272 | to be charged pro rata against the value of all the shares entitled to an appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) of this section or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction under subsection (k) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(j) (src:1272)
GIVEN `the expenses the Court ordered to be charged` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the person's shares entitled to appraisal` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 262(j) the person's pro rata share of the expenses charged against the shares` `the expenses the Court ordered to be charged` `the value of the person's shares entitled to appraisal` `the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF       `the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction` AT MOST 0
          OR `the value of the person's shares entitled to appraisal` LESS THAN 0
          OR `the value of the person's shares entitled to appraisal` GREATER THAN `the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the expenses the Court ordered to be charged` TIMES (`the value of the person's shares entitled to appraisal` DIVIDED BY `the value of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed pursuant to subsection (k) or subject to such an award pursuant to a reservation of jurisdiction`))

§ `s 262(k) The person who has demanded appraisal: no vote, no dividends, withdrawal and lapse`

-- "Subject to the remainder of this subsection, from and after the effective date ..., no person who has demanded appraisal rights
-- with respect to some or all of such person's shares as provided in subsection (d) of this section shall be entitled to vote such
-- shares for any purpose or to receive payment of dividends or other distributions on such shares (except dividends or other
-- distributions payable to stockholders of record at a date which is prior to the effective date ...)."
-- The text does not say whether the bar lifts when the right to appraisal has ceased by withdrawal or lapse ("subject to the
-- remainder of this subsection" does not say how): that case answers NOTHING (not covered), fork F-k1.
-- src:1273 | Subject to the remainder of this subsection, from and after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, no person who has demanded appraisal rights with respect to some or all of such person’s shares as provided in subsection (d) of this section shall be entitled to vote such shares for any purpose or to receive payment of dividends or other distributions on such shares (except dividends or other distributions payable to stockholders of record at a date which is prior to the effective date …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(k) (src:1273)
GIVEN `the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the vote` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(k) the person is barred from voting the shares` `the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares` `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` `the date of the vote` `the effective date` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares` AND `the date of the vote` AT LEAST `the effective date`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1273 | Subject to the remainder of this subsection, from and after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, no person who has demanded appraisal rights with respect to some or all of such person’s shares as provided in subsection (d) of this section shall be entitled to vote such shares for any purpose or to receive payment of dividends or other distributions on such shares (except dividends or other distributions payable to stockholders of record at a date which is prior to the effective date …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(k) (src:1273)
GIVEN `the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the dividend or distribution is paid` IS A DATE
      `the record date of the dividend or distribution` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(k) the person is barred from receiving the dividend or distribution on the shares` `the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares` `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` `the date the dividend or distribution is paid` `the record date of the dividend or distribution` `the effective date` MEANS
    IF NOT (       `the person has demanded appraisal rights with respect to the shares`
             AND `the date the dividend or distribution is paid` AT LEAST `the effective date`
             AND `the record date of the dividend or distribution` AT LEAST `the effective date`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the right to appraisal of the shares has since ceased` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "If a person who has made a demand for an appraisal in accordance with this section shall deliver to the surviving, resulting or
-- converted entity a written withdrawal of such person's demand for an appraisal in respect of some or all of such person's shares in
-- accordance with subsection (e) of this section, either within 60 days after such effective date or thereafter with the written
-- approval of the corporation, then the right of such person to an appraisal of the shares subject to the withdrawal shall cease."
-- src:1273 | If a person who has made a demand for an appraisal in accordance with this section shall deliver to the surviving, resulting or converted entity a written withdrawal of such person’s demand for an appraisal in respect of some or all of such person’s shares in accordance with subsection (e) of this section, either within 60 days after such effective date or thereafter with the written approval of the corporation, then the right of such person to an appraisal of the shares subject to the withdrawal shall cease …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(k) (src:1273)
GIVEN `the person delivered a written withdrawal of the demand to the surviving, resulting or converted entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the withdrawal was delivered` IS A DATE
      `the corporation approved the withdrawal in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(k) the right of the person to an appraisal of the shares subject to the withdrawal ceases` `the person delivered a written withdrawal of the demand to the surviving, resulting or converted entity` `the date the withdrawal was delivered` `the corporation approved the withdrawal in writing` `the effective date` MEANS
        `the person delivered a written withdrawal of the demand to the surviving, resulting or converted entity`
    AND (   `the date the withdrawal was delivered` AT MOST `the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the effective date`
         OR `the corporation approved the withdrawal in writing`)

-- "Notwithstanding the foregoing, an appraisal proceeding in the Court of Chancery shall not be dismissed as to any person without the
-- approval of the Court, and such approval may be conditioned upon such terms as the Court deems just ...; provided, however that this
-- provision shall not affect the right of any person who has not commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined that proceeding as a named
-- party to withdraw such person's demand for appraisal and to accept the terms offered ... within 60 days after the effective date".
-- src:1273 | Notwithstanding the foregoing, an appraisal proceeding in the Court of Chancery shall not be dismissed as to any person without the approval of the Court, and such approval may be conditioned upon such terms as the Court deems just, including without limitation, a reservation of jurisdiction for any application to the Court made under subsection (j) of this section; provided, however that this provision shall not affect the right of any person who has not commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined that proceeding as a named party to withdraw such person’s demand for appraisal and to accept the terms offered upon the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance within 60 days after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, as set forth in subsection (e) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(k) (src:1273)
GIVEN `the person has commenced the appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(k) the proceeding cannot be dismissed as to the person without the approval of the Court` `the person has commenced the appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party` MEANS
    `the person has commenced the appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party`

-- "If a petition for an appraisal is not filed within the time provided in subsection (e) of this section, the right to appraisal with
-- respect to all shares shall cease." The time is 120 days after the effective date, the 120th day inside it (fork F-d1).
-- Asked on a given day: a right does not cease before the last day for a petition has passed; once it has, it has ceased unless a petition was
-- filed by that day.
-- src:1273 | If a petition for an appraisal is not filed within the time provided in subsection (e) of this section, the right to appraisal with respect to all shares shall cease …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(k) (src:1273)
GIVEN `the date the first petition was filed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(k) the right to appraisal with respect to all shares has ceased for want of a petition` `the date the first petition was filed` `the effective date` `the date on which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the first petition was filed`
    WHEN JUST filed THEN filed GREATER THAN `s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date`

§ `s 262(l) The status of the shares that would have been issued`

-- "The shares or other equity interests of the surviving, resulting or converted entity to which the shares of stock subject to
-- appraisal under this section would have otherwise converted but for an appraisal demand made in accordance with this section shall
-- have the status of authorized but not outstanding shares of stock or other equity interests of the surviving, resulting or converted
-- entity, unless and until the person that has demanded appraisal is no longer entitled to appraisal pursuant to this section."
-- src:1274 | The shares or other equity interests of the surviving, resulting or converted entity to which the shares of stock subject to appraisal under this section would have otherwise converted but for an appraisal demand made in accordance with this section shall have the status of authorized but not outstanding shares of stock or other equity interests of the surviving, resulting or converted entity, unless and until the person that has demanded appraisal is no longer entitled to appraisal pursuant to this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(l) (src:1274)
GIVEN `an appraisal demand was made in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person that demanded appraisal is still entitled to appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(l) the shares or equity interests have the status of authorized but not outstanding` `an appraisal demand was made in accordance with this section` `the person that demanded appraisal is still entitled to appraisal` MEANS
        `an appraisal demand was made in accordance with this section`
    AND `the person that demanded appraisal is still entitled to appraisal`
